{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Dialogue State Tracking Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: rule-based slot extractor"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "See `code/main.py`. Regex + synonym dictionaries cover 70% of canonical utterances in narrow domains:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "CUISINE_SYNONYMS = {"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"italian\": [\"italian\", \"pasta\", \"pizza\", \"italy\"],"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"chinese\": [\"chinese\", \"chow mein\", \"noodles\"],"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def extract_cuisine(utterance):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for canonical, synonyms in CUISINE_SYNONYMS.items():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if any(syn in utterance.lower() for syn in synonyms):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            return canonical"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return None"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Brittle outside the canonical vocabulary. Works for deterministic slot confirmations."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: state update loop"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def update_state(state, utterance):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    new_state = dict(state)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for slot, extractor in SLOT_EXTRACTORS.items():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        value = extractor(utterance)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if value is not None:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            new_state[slot] = value"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for slot in NEGATION_CLEARS:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if is_negated(utterance, slot):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            new_state[slot] = None"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return new_state"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Three invariants:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- Never reset a slot the user did not touch."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- Explicit negation (\"never mind the cuisine\") must clear."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- User correction (\"actually...\") must overwrite, not append."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: LLM-driven DST with structured output"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from pydantic import BaseModel"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from typing import Literal, Optional"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import instructor"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class RestaurantState(BaseModel):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    cuisine: Optional[Literal[\"italian\", \"chinese\", \"indian\", \"thai\", \"any\"]] = None"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    area: Optional[Literal[\"north\", \"south\", \"east\", \"west\", \"center\"]] = None"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    price: Optional[Literal[\"cheap\", \"moderate\", \"expensive\"]] = None"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    people: Optional[int] = None"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    day: Optional[str] = None"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def llm_dst(history, llm):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    prompt = f\"\"\"You track the slot values of a restaurant booking across turns."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Dialogue so far:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "{render(history)}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Update the state based on the latest user turn. Output only the JSON state.\"\"\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return llm(prompt, response_model=RestaurantState)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Instructor + Pydantic guarantees a valid state object. No regex, no schema mismatches, no hallucinated slots."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: JGA evaluation"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def joint_goal_accuracy(predicted_states, gold_states):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    correct = sum(1 for p, g in zip(predicted_states, gold_states) if p == g)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return correct / len(predicted_states)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Calibrate: what fraction of turns does the system get ALL slots right? For MultiWOZ 2.4, top 2026 systems: 80-83%. Your in-domain system should exceed that on your narrow vocabulary or the LLM baseline beats you."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 5: handling correction"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "CORRECTION_CUES = {\"actually\", \"no wait\", \"on second thought\", \"change that to\"}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def is_correction(utterance):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return any(cue in utterance.lower() for cue in CORRECTION_CUES)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "On a detected correction, overwrite the last-updated slot rather than appending. Hard to get right without LLM help. The modern pattern: always let the LLM regenerate the whole state from history rather than incrementally updating \u2014 this naturally handles corrections."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. **Easy.** Build the rule-based state tracker in `code/main.py` for 3 slots (cuisine, area, price). Test on 10 hand-crafted dialogues. Measure JGA.\n2. **Medium.** Same dataset with Instructor + Pydantic + a small LLM. Compare JGA. Inspect the hardest turns.\n3. **Hard.** Implement both and route: rule-based primary, LLM fallback when rule-based emits <2 slots with confidence. Measure the combined JGA and inference cost per turn."
      ]
    }
